  "agent": {
    "note": "BEAT 3 — top-contributors, built on pulse-chrome (same BEAT chip / FFmpeg logo / title / subtitle / footer / baked scatter / bg-first timing as Beats 1-2). Main panel = the locked @m0saic/alpine/contributor-table/v1 (showHeader:false — the chrome owns the title), green +additions / red -deletions diff. Rail = aggregate stat-cards from pulse.contributors.rail. Aspect-adaptive: DESKTOP table-left + 1x4 rail-right; SQUARE table-top + 2x2 rail-below; MOBILE the table reflows to its portrait stacked-card layout + a 2x2 rail below. Fixed the title clip per-variant (TOP CONTRIBUTORS is longer than the other beats; widened the box on desktop, trimmed title height on square/mobile — capFont em is shared so I tuned geometry instead). Renders: /tmp/b3d2.mp4 (desktop), /tmp/b3s2.mp4 (square), /tmp/b3m2.mp4 (mobile). Open here in Make to scrub + switch aspect.",
    "question": "Beat 3 good across desktop / square / mobile? Watch for: title sizing vs Beats 1-2 (square/mobile title is a touch smaller to fit the longer headline — or I can shorten the headline to CONTRIBUTORS to keep the big consistent font), the 1x4 vs 2x2 rail choice on desktop, mobile rail tile proportions (wide-short), and the table/rail balance.",
